 ## Account Withdrawal Rules — sample .spectable file (v2.7.2 syntax)
#
#Spe Acification Account Withdrawal Rules
#Description Defines rules and scenarios for withdrawing money from accounts.
#Details \
#  Covers checking and savings withdrawals. \
#  Includes data types, business rules, calculations, and scenarios.
#
## ============================================================
## Define — reusable values and tables
## ============================================================
#
#Define StandardFee = 35
#Define SavingsFee = 25
#
#
#
#
#
## ============================================================
## Attributes (standalone, reused across rules and scenarios)
## ============================================================
#
#Attributes WithdrawalInput
#Description Input data for a withdrawal operation.
#| Attribute | Type   | Default | Notes             | In-Out |
#| Amount    | Dollar | 0       | Withdrawal amount | In     |
#
#Attributes BalanceCheck
#Description Output data for verifying resulting account balance.
#| Attribute | Type    | Default | Notes             | In-Out |
#| Balance   | Dollar  | 0       | Resulting balance | Out    |
#| Valid     | Boolean | false   | Balance is valid  | Out    |
#
## ============================================================
## Business Rules
## ============================================================
#
#
## ============================================================
## Calculations
## ============================================================
#
#Calculation NetBalance
#Description Computes the net balance remaining after subtracting any fee.
#Details \
#  NetBalance = Balance - Fee \
#  A negative result indicates the account is overdrawn.
#Examples: NetBalanceData
#| Balance | Fee | NetBalance | Notes          |
#| 100     | 0   | 100        | No fee applied |
#| 100     | 1   | 99         | Small fee      |
#| -50     | 25  | -75        | Overdrawn case |
#Attributes NetBalanceData
#| Attribute  | Type   | Default | Notes | In-Out |
#| Balance    | Dollar | 0       |       | In     |
#| Fee        | Dollar | 0       |       | In     |
#| NetBalance | Dollar | 0       |       | Out    |
#
## ============================================================
## Background (shared setup for all scenarios in this file)
## ============================================================
#
#Background:
#Description Pre-loaded accounts available to all scenarios.
#Given accounts exist in the system: Account
#| Type     | Balance | AccountID |
#| Checking | 100     | 123-456   |
#| Savings  | 200     | 987-654   |
#
## ============================================================
## Scenarios
## ============================================================
#
#Scenario Withdraw exact balance from checking
#Description Withdrawing the full checking balance leaves a zero balance.
#Given checking account: Account Vertical
#| Type      | Checking |
#| Balance   | 100      |
#| AccountID | 123-456  |
#When withdrawal is submitted: WithdrawalInput Vertical
#| Amount | 100 |
#Then balance is zero: BalanceCheck Vertical
#| Balance | 0    |
#| Valid   | true |
#
#Scenario Withdraw using defined account data
#Description Uses a Define table reference for the account setup.
#Given checking account: Account Vertical
#=DefaultAccount
#When withdrawal is submitted: WithdrawalInput Vertical
#| Amount | 50 |
#Then balance is correct: BalanceCheck Vertical
#| Balance | 50   |
#| Valid   | true |
#
#ScenarioGroup Overdraft Scenarios
#Description Scenarios where the withdrawal exceeds the available balance.
#Details \
#  Covers checking and savings overdraft cases. \
#  Verifies the correct fee is applied per account type.
#
#Scenario Overdraft on checking account
#Description Withdrawing more than the balance triggers a $35 overdraft fee.
#Given overdrawn checking account: Account Vertical
#=OverdrawnAccount
#When overdraft fee is applied: WithdrawalInput
#| Amount |
#| 0      |
#Then fee is correct: BalanceCheck
#| Balance | Valid |
#| -85     | false |
## Balance -50, fee =StandardFee 
#
#Scenario Overdraft on savings account
#Description Withdrawing more than the savings balance triggers a $25 overdraft fee.
#Given savings account has low balance: Account
#| Type    | Balance | AccountID |
#| Savings | 30      | 987-654   |
#When withdrawal exceeds balance: WithdrawalInput
#| Amount |
#| 80     |
#Then overdraft fee is applied: BalanceCheck
#| Balance | Valid |
#| -75     | false |
#
## ============================================================
## Directives
## ============================================================
#
#Import "common-types.spectable"
#Description Imports shared DataType definitions used across specifications.
#
#Insert "../data/accounts.csv"
#Description Inserts reference account data for documentation purposes.
